{
  "name": "reply-forward-options",
  "description": "replyToMessage and forwardMessage options on seeded messages (POP3 Inbox and Local Folders Sent). Direct sending is allowed for this scenario only (blockSkipReview = false). Reply drafts: the recipients Thunderbird computes (sender, Reply-To, reply all with the other To and Cc recipients without the user's own address, Mail-Followup-To, a mailing-list post), explicit to, cc, bcc and from, attachments (inline and by path), an HTML reply, threading headers and the quote; latestInThread answers the newest message of the conversation, here the user's own answer in Sent (repliedTo says so), or the message itself when it is the newest; a reply to an own message goes to its recipients. Forward drafts: to, cc, bcc, an intro, the original's attachment, X-Forwarded-Message-Id, an HTML intro with no recipient. Direct modes: a reply and a forward sent to the local mailpit sink with their headers, quote, forwarded and extra attachments. Errors: latestInThread with send, send without to or from, a direct reply or forward of an encrypted message, a message with no subject, unknown message or folder, unknown sender identity, a refused attachment path. Not covered: the compose window of a reply or forward (see compose-options.json), several identities (the lab has one), a message without Message-ID. Nothing else is sent.",
  "prefs": {
    "mail.server.server2.directory-rel": "[ProfD]Mail/127.0.0.1",
    "extensions.commonpost-mcp.blockSkipReview": false
  },
  "schema_watch": [
    "replyToMessage",
    "forwardMessage"
  ],
